-- title:
--   Crossing points rational over an algebraically closed residue field
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0\ge 1$ and a prime $p$ with $p\nmid N_0$, and let `𝔓 : DRModelPackageLevel N₀ p hpN₀` be a Deligne–Rapoport model package at level $N_0p$ over the base ring `DRLevel.R p`. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain equipped with a ring homomorphism $\rho_O$ from `DRLevel.R p`, whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$, and whose residue field is algebraically closed; let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ with decidable equality, and $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ a ring homomorphism. The assertion is that for every point $x$ of the fibre product of the two morphisms `𝔓.comp κ (toκ.comp ρO) 0` and `𝔓.comp κ (toκ.comp ρO) 1` furnished by the package for the composite $\mathrm{to}\kappa\circ\rho_O$, there is a morphism $s$ from $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue field of $O$ to `DRLevel.fibre` of $(\mathrm{residue}\ O)\circ\rho_O$, that is to the base change of the model `X N₀ p` along the residue map, such that $s$ followed by the second projection is the identity (so $s$ is a section over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue field), and such that the two points of the underlying space of `XO ρO` agree: the image under the base map of `DRLevel.bcMap ρO toκ` of the image of $x$ under the first projection followed by `𝔓.comp κ (toκ.comp ρO) 0`, and the image under the base map of `DRLevel.bcMap ρO (IsLocalRing.residue O)` of the value of $s$ at the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue field.
--
--   This is the rationality statement for the crossing points of the fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0p)$ in characteristic $p$: read over the model over $O$, every such point of the $\kappa$-fibre is already the image of a point with values in the (algebraically closed) residue field of $O$. It feeds the construction of the resolved model package at level $N_0p$, where the crossing points and their coordinates are used to identify the node structure of the special fibre.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRModelPackageLevel_exists_residueField_point_baseChangeMap_eq_of_isAlgClosed_residueField.lean

